## §Content-Equivalence Verdict Doctrine — git patch-id --stable + Lane 3 d-test-only sign-off (per RETRO-032 lesson #10, cycle ~#3642H)

When the PR under review contains a d-test authored/edited but the implementation has NOT yet landed in this PR (Phase A/B split, forward-port cluster, or sister-PR-elsewhere), the tester MUST verify via **content equivalence** rather than waiting for live impl. This is the canonical Lane 3 d-test-only sign-off path.

### The doctrine — three pillars

1. **`git patch-id --stable` content equivalence**: When implementation lives in a sister-PR (cross-repo, separate cluster-squash member, or v3 amendment), compute `git patch-id --stable` on the d-test patch and the impl patch. Matching patch-id = content-equivalent regardless of git commit-graph ancestry (defeats `gh repo create --template` synthetic-init fragmentation, cycle ~#3682 Defect #2).
2. **Lane 3 d-test-only sign-off (RED state OK)**: A d-test in RED state (4/8 PASS + 4/8 FAIL with FAIL being pre-impl unimplemented) IS a valid sign-off when Cadence Rule 1 atomic honored + d-test isolation guards (FIXTURE_MODE hooks, NOT live API calls) + cross-reference anchors verified. RED is the canonical Phase A pattern, NOT a defect.
3. **PR #1178 v3 amendment pattern**: when `gh repo create --template` synthetic-init breaks commit-graph equivalence (strict-equal ✗, descendant-of ✗), content-equivalence via blob SHA `git hash-object <file>` is the trust-but-verify fallback (sister-pattern cycle ~#3940Q+9 + cycle ~#3955Q).

### Pre-flight (Issue #414 + RETRO-005 #26 compatible)

- **Layer 2 REST quartet re-query** of the sister-PR(s) — `gh pr view <N>` for state + mergedAt + mergeCommit + closingIssuesReferences
- **`git patch-id --stable`** on d-test patch + impl patch — must match
- **`git hash-object`** on blob-equivalent files when patch-id unavailable (file-level content SHA)
- **Cadence Rule 1 atomic** verified (single commit covers d-test + INDEX.md row + CHANGELOG if applicable)
- **d-test isolation** verified (FIXTURE_MODE hooks, NOT live API — sister-pattern d001 S29-013)
- **Cross-reference anchors** verified (Refs/Closes anchors point to real PRs/Issues in correct repo)

### Lane 3 verdict comment header

Cite `cycle ~#3642H` + `RETRO-032 lesson #10` + `git patch-id --stable` + `Lane 3 d-test-only sign-off (RED state OK)`. The header enables RETRO-007 audit grep for Lane 3 sign-off precedent.

### Anti-patterns

- ❌ Refusing verdict on a RED-state d-test when Cadence Rule 1 + isolation guards + cross-refs all satisfied — this stalls sister-PR cluster-squash sequences indefinitely
- ❌ Trusting commit-graph strict-equality or descendant-of over `gh repo create --template` synthetic-init — synthetic-init fragmentation is the cycle ~#3682 Defect #2 root cause
- ❌ Lane 3 sign-off WITHOUT `git patch-id --stable` or blob-SHA content equivalence — must be one of the two content-blob evidence types
- ❌ Skipping the Lane 3 verdict comment header citation — defeats RETRO-007 audit grep pattern

